Fix non-serialization AOT warnings in `/tmp/sv-f64936991a204d3da269e906b81dc889/before/`. Make the following specific changes:

## Rules
- Do NOT use `#pragma warning disable` or `[UnconditionalSuppressMessage]` for any IL warning.

## 1. ArmOperation.cs
Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` annotation to the `T` generic parameter on `IsResource<T>()`, `Rehydrate<T>()`, and `RehydrateAsync<T>()`.

The `IsResource<T>` method uses `typeof(T).GetConstructor(BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance, ...)` and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance, ...)`. Both require `NonPublicConstructors`.

Changes:
- Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` if not present
- Change `private static bool IsResource<T>() where T : notnull` to `private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull`
- Change `public static ArmOperation<T> Rehydrate<T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull` to `public static ArmOperation<T> Rehydrate<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull`
- Change `public static async Task<ArmOperation<T>> RehydrateAsync<T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull` to `public static async Task<ArmOperation<T>> RehydrateAsync<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull`

Note: `IsResource<T>` is only called from `Rehydrate<T>` and `RehydrateAsync<T>` which are the public entry points.

## 2. GenericOperationSource.cs
The class `GenericOperationSource<T>` uses `ModelReaderWriter.Read(response.Content, typeof(T))` which requires `PublicConstructors | NonPublicConstructors`, and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance, ...)` which requires `NonPublicConstructors`.

Changes:
- Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` if not already present (it is present on line 8)
- Change `internal class GenericOperationSource<T> : IOperationSource<T>` to `internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>`

## 3. ArmEnvironment.cs (line 80)
Replace `JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)` with manual JSON writing. The struct has 3 public properties: `Endpoint` (Uri), `Audience` (string), `DefaultScope` (string).

Change line 80 from:
```csharp
public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);
```
to:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    var buffer = new System.Buffers.ArrayBufferWriter<byte>();
    using (var writer = new Utf8JsonWriter(buffer))
    {
        writer.WriteStartObject();
        writer.WriteString(nameof(Endpoint), Endpoint.ToString());
        writer.WriteString(nameof(Audience), Audience);
        writer.WriteString(nameof(DefaultScope), DefaultScope);
        writer.WriteEndObject();
    }
    return System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(buffer.WrittenSpan);
}
```

## 4. ArmClientOptions.cs (line 52)
Replace `JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span)` with `JsonDocument` parsing.

The current code at lines 48-78:
```csharp
var assembly = Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly();
using (Stream stream = assembly.GetManifestResourceStream(profile.GetManifestName()))
{
    var span = BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span;
    var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);
    var armProfile = allProfile["resource-manager"];
    foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile)
    {
        var namespaceName = keyValuePair.Key;
        var element = keyValuePair.Value;
        // ... rest iterates element.EnumerateObject()
    }
}
```

Replace lines 51-53 (the span + JsonSerializer + armProfile lines) with:
```csharp
using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));
var armProfile = doc.RootElement.GetProperty("resource-manager");
```

Then change `foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile)` to `foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile.EnumerateObject())` and `keyValuePair.Key` to `keyValuePair.Name`, and `keyValuePair.Value` should become a `JsonElement` (which is already what it is - `JsonElement element = keyValuePair.Value`).

Wait - the existing code uses `element.EnumerateObject()` already on line 59. So when `element` was `JsonElement` from a `Dictionary<string, JsonElement>` value, it would be enumerable. With our change, `keyValuePair.Value` is also a `JsonElement`, so `element` stays the same.

So the changes are:
1. Remove the `var span = BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span;` line
2. Change `var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);` to `using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));`
3. Change `var armProfile = allProfile["resource-manager"];` to `var armProfile = doc.RootElement.GetProperty("resource-manager");`
4. Change `foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile)` to `foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile.EnumerateObject())`
5. Change `keyValuePair.Key` to `keyValuePair.Name`
6. Change `var element = keyValuePair.Value;` - this can stay since the property `Value` returns `JsonElement` for both `JsonProperty` and `KeyValuePair`

## 5. Extensions/ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs (line 30)
The method calls `builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration)` which is from `IAzureClientFactoryBuilderWithConfiguration` and is annotated with `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]`. 

Add `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]` to the `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` method:

```csharp
